* Some web sites are saying as much as 100 watts, but at 2000 Calories a  
day, the human body has only 97 watts total.  Assuming the brain uses 20%  
of that, it gets 19 watts of power.  So where I live it costs $1.09 a  
month to run a human brain on electricity, or $5.59 for the whole body.   
It makes food seem so expensive.

